            {"heading": "Reading a Job Offer Beyond the Number", "body": "When an offer comes in, the hourly wage or salary is only part of the picture. Schedule flexibility, distance from home, opportunities to grow, and whether the environment felt respectful during the interview all matter too. It's reasonable to ask for a day to think it over before accepting, and reasonable to ask questions about schedule or training before saying yes. Rushing into the first offer without thinking it through can lead to regret a few weeks in."},
